# D2 — Dated tables on source-of-record guides

When a page states a **statutory or official indexed number** (HSM salary floors, IND fees, 30% norms/cap, minimum wage, eigen risico, toeslagen parameters, etc.):

1. Show a visible **last-reviewed** date above the fold (hero).
2. Show at least one **official source link** above the fold (hero).
3. **Do not strip** FAQs, dated tables, or other citability layers when editing.

Prefer `GuideHeroTrustMeta` (`src/components/guides/GuideHeroTrustMeta.tsx`) or `GuidePageTemplate`’s `lastUpdated` + `heroOfficialSources` contract.

Source-of-record examples: 30% ruling, minimum wage, health insurance (early setup + comparison), BSN, HSM, `/netherlands/official-figures/`.
